nt.com/u/11568491?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie","html_url":"https://github.com/PingXie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T23:42:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T23:42:24Z","body":"all, I have incorporated all the feedback and made the following changes\r\n\r\n1. categorize major decisions into two buckets: technical and governance\r\n2. technical decisions by default go with a simple majority vote but if 2 weeks go by without a veto, +2 is acceptable. \r\n3. no more retraction. any motions on previous +2 decisions should go with their own \"technical major decision\" process, which include notifying the entire tsc team as well.\r\n4. all governance changes with the exception of \"inactive members\" now require 2/3 votes. removing \"inactive members\" requires simple majority only. this is to prevent a rare case where more than 1/3 of TSC members going through some major life changes and we don't end up in a limbo state wherein we lose quorum forever.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valkey-io/valkey/issues/comments/3644253546/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valkey-io/valkey/issues/comments/3644256009","html_url":"https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey/pull/2927#issuecomment-3644256009","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/valkey-io/valkey/issues/2927","id":3644256009,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLjzmI87ZNu8J","user":{"login":"PingXie","id":11568491,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTY4NDkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11568491?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie","html_url":"https://github.com/PingXie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PingXie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-11T23:43:28Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T23:43:28Z","body":"> Regarding the top comment.\r\n> \r\n> > Add +2 mechanism for technical major decisions\r\n> > Add 1/3 organization limit for TSC membership\r\n> \r\n> I feel these two might conflict with each other. Though all the TSC member are working in the best interest of the community, I believe we don't want a single organization to force the direction of the project. Hence, the 1/3 organization limit on TSC membership. If the project starts adding members from the same organization of current TSC members, won't there be major decisions made without requiring others input/suggestion.\r\n\r\n@hpatro can you please re-review the latest update? I have consolidated all governance decisions on 2/3 (with the exception of removing inactive members)","aut